{"reply":"No. These sources make team climate a possibility to consider, but they don’t prove it caused your silence or that anyone would have done the same.

In Chapter 8, “The Queen’s Croquet-Ground,” the gardeners paint the white roses red to cover the wrong tree and say they fear what will happen if the Queen finds out: “if the Queen was to find it out, we should all have our heads cut off, you know.” That’s a parallel involving anticipated punishment, not evidence about your team.

Your note says the billing mistake was yours, you fixed it over the weekend, said nothing Monday, and keep telling yourself it was already handled. It doesn’t identify why you stayed quiet or whether your team punishes mistakes. A cross-sectional study of hospital nurses and nurse managers reports that leader inclusiveness, safety climate, and psychological safety significantly affected willingness to report errors ([study](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10599306/)). That finding can’t establish what caused your silence or how everyone would respond. What, if anything, do you remember weighing most at the time?","evidence_uses":[{"source_kind":"book_corpus","evidence_id":"pg11-v01b38ea4-ch08-ln1931-1970","source_location":"Chapter 8 — The Queen’s Croquet-Ground, source lines 1931-1970","exact_quote":"if the Queen was to find it out, we should all have our heads cut off, you know.","supported_claims":["In Chapter 8, “The Queen’s Croquet-Ground,” the gardeners paint the white roses red to cover the wrong tree and say they fear what will happen if the Queen finds out: “if the Queen was to find it out, we should all have our heads cut off, you know.”"],"limit_claims":["That’s a parallel involving anticipated punishment, not evidence about your team."]},{"source_kind":"memory","evidence_id":"mem_59454a1a72071acadee96f58d8954147163381934693585ce06450459b821504","supported_claims":["Your note says the billing mistake was yours, you fixed it over the weekend, said nothing Monday, and keep telling yourself it was already handled."],"limit_claims":["It doesn’t identify why you stayed quiet or whether your team punishes mistakes."]},{"source_kind":"web","evidence_id":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10599306/","supported_claims":["A cross-sectional study of hospital nurses and nurse managers reports that leader inclusiveness, safety climate, and psychological safety significantly affected willingness to report errors"],"limit_claims":["That finding can’t est